There's a fucking bus down there.

259
00:13:01,782 --> 00:13:03,695
God knows how many people with zero idea

260
00:13:03,697 --> 00:13:05,839
of the shit storm they just rolled into.

261
00:13:05,841 --> 00:13:07,090
How do you think they're gonna react

262
00:13:07,092 --> 00:13:09,021
when we tell them they can't leave?

263
00:13:10,731 --> 00:13:12,133
Look.

264
00:13:12,317 --> 00:13:14,544
We have a long night ahead of us.

265
00:13:14,976 --> 00:13:18,107
Boyd picked one hell of
a time to go on safari.

266
00:13:18,564 --> 00:13:22,880
If this shit goes sideways,
you have to be ready to step up.

267
00:13:22,882 --> 00:13:24,169
You got that?

268
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:26,661
You're sheriff now.

269
00:13:27,623 --> 00:13:28,857
- Kristi?
- Yeah?

270
00:13:28,859 --> 00:13:31,122
Grab your stuff.
Meet us down at the diner.

271
00:13:31,124 --> 00:13:33,247
We're about to make some new friends.

272
00:13:33,249 --> 00:13:35,879
[PASSENGER LAUGHING]

273
00:13:35,881 --> 00:13:37,238
It's locked.

274
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:41,250
[LAUGHS, WHOOPS]

275
00:13:42,802 --> 00:13:44,560
Fuckin' shirt.

276
00:13:45,438 --> 00:13:49,638
You all, come join me!

277
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:51,817
Ha ha!

278
00:13:51,819 --> 00:13:55,286
Whoo! Whoo!

279
00:13:58,412 --> 00:14:02,708
- Oh, the sun! Ha ha ha!
- No way.

280
00:14:02,710 --> 00:14:05,974
Ah. Rain dance is done.

281
00:14:07,027 --> 00:14:09,647
Just follow my finger with your eyes.

282
00:14:09,902 --> 00:14:11,622
Good.

283
00:14:11,624 --> 00:14:14,067
Great. Okay. Can I see your hand?

284
00:14:17,467 --> 00:14:19,117
Okay, pulse is good.

285
00:14:20,055 --> 00:14:21,755
No sign of a fever.

286
00:14:21,790 --> 00:14:24,247
Look, I need everybody off the bus.

287
00:14:24,419 --> 00:14:26,049
Seriously?

288
00:14:26,051 --> 00:14:28,966
Just give us a minute. Please?

289
00:14:30,848 --> 00:14:33,198
You a doctor or something?

290
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:35,140
Pediatric nurse.

291
00:14:35,245 --> 00:14:36,403
Oh.

292
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:38,270
Hey.

293
00:14:38,478 --> 00:14:40,058
Hey, what's your name?

294
00:14:43,252 --> 00:14:44,505
Elgin.

295
00:14:44,507 --> 00:14:45,708
Elgin?

296
00:14:46,692 --> 00:14:48,482
Elgin, do you know where you are?

297
00:14:50,317 --> 00:14:51,747
Do you?

298
00:14:52,847 --> 00:14:54,896
Why were you screaming like that?

299
00:14:58,523 --> 00:15:01,668
I had a really bad dream.

300
00:15:01,868 --> 00:15:03,755
Hey. Hey, what the fuck was that?

301
00:15:03,757 --> 00:15:05,247
- Hey.
- Back off, man.

302
00:15:05,249 --> 00:15:07,567
Why don't you back off? I'm the one
with fuckin' puke on my shirt.

303
00:15:07,630 --> 00:15:09,560
What the fuck is wrong with you?

304
00:15:09,767 --> 00:15:11,200
I'm sorry.

305
00:15:11,991 --> 00:15:13,224
You're a goddamn freak.

306
00:15:13,226 --> 00:15:16,341
Let's give him some space, okay?

307
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,281
- Excuse me.
- You alright, man?

308
00:15:24,588 --> 00:15:26,781
Smells fuckin' terrible in here.

309
00:15:27,790 --> 00:15:29,150
Asshole.

310
00:15:29,152 --> 00:15:30,640
Hey, cut the guy a break.

311
00:15:30,642 --> 00:15:32,093
Do you wanna go outside?

312
00:15:34,620 --> 00:15:36,190
Elgin?

313
00:15:38,550 --> 00:15:41,430
How about I just sit here
with you until you're ready?

314
00:15:41,695 --> 00:15:43,100
Okay?

315
00:15:46,706 --> 00:15:48,406
Okay.

316
00:15:53,972 --> 00:15:55,972
[PANTS]

317
00:15:57,478 --> 00:15:58,748
Oh, my God.

318
00:15:59,018 --> 00:16:00,562
Julie! Hey.

319
00:16:00,564 --> 00:16:02,194
- I need to find my dad.
- Wait, wait, wait.

320
00:16:02,196 --> 00:16:04,776
Ellis! Pretty crazy, huh?

321
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:06,976
Maybe the magic tower summoned them.

322
00:16:08,222 --> 00:16:09,672
You ever see something like this?

323
00:16:09,674 --> 00:16:12,044
- Dad? Dad?
- Nope. These people are fucked.

324
00:16:12,158 --> 00:16:14,796
Everybody? Everybody gather round.

325
00:16:14,798 --> 00:16:17,554
Gather round. Just
want y'all to sit tight.

326
00:16:17,556 --> 00:16:20,092
I'm gonna clean things up in
there and we'll be on our way.

327
00:16:20,094 --> 00:16:21,945
- Hi. Hey.
- Hi.

328
00:16:21,947 --> 00:16:23,515
Uh, listen.

329
00:16:23,517 --> 00:16:25,132
There's gonna be a bunch
of people on their way down.

330
00:16:25,134 --> 00:16:26,554
- Mmm.
- Um...

331
00:16:26,556 --> 00:16:28,396
And they're gonna help
you guys out, alright?

332
00:16:28,398 --> 00:16:30,367
So we'll get the diner unlocked,

333
00:16:30,369 --> 00:16:32,007
and we'll get you guys sorted out.

334
00:16:32,009 --> 00:16:33,890
Okay, well, this isn't a pit stop, okay?

335
00:16:33,892 --> 00:16:37,367
So unless you have a mop,
I'm good. Thanks.

336
00:16:39,719 --> 00:16:41,531
Holy shit.

337
00:16:42,358 --> 00:16:43,418
What happened?

338
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:45,273
- The floor just...
- JIM: I don't know.

339
00:16:48,023 --> 00:16:49,462
Where's Mom?

340
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:52,756
I, uh... Ethan?

341
00:16:52,758 --> 00:16:54,039
Uh, where's Ethan?

342
00:16:54,041 --> 00:16:55,778
[STAMMERS]: He's fine. He's at Colony.

343
00:16:55,780 --> 00:16:57,026
Dad, is she down there?

344
00:16:57,028 --> 00:16:59,382
Julie, listen to me.

345
00:16:59,643 --> 00:17:01,492
I need you to get help, okay?

346
00:17:01,494 --> 00:17:03,414
Get as many people as you can.

347
00:17:04,187 --> 00:17:05,627
Julie!

348
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:12,000
Okay. All right. Come here. Come here.

349
00:17:12,002 --> 00:17:14,142
[CRIES]

350
00:17:17,494 --> 00:17:20,250
Now is the time for you to be strong.

351
00:17:20,536 --> 00:17:22,628
Your mom needs you, okay?

352
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:24,610
Go and get help.

353
00:17:24,819 --> 00:17:26,789
- Okay.
- Go. Now.

354
00:17:33,528 --> 00:17:35,538
- You sure you're okay?
- Oh, yeah. I'm fine.

355
00:17:35,540 --> 00:17:37,179
- Okay. Just let me know...
- JULIE: Ellis!

356
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:38,461
What's wrong?

357
00:17:38,463 --> 00:17:40,258
- It's my mom. She's trapped.
- Wait, wait. What?

358
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:42,031
She was digging in the
basement. My dad's inside.

359
00:17:42,033 --> 00:17:44,868
- She needs help. Please.
- Whoa, whoa. Stay with the bus.

360
00:17:44,870 --> 00:17:46,658
- I got this.
- You sure?

361
00:17:46,660 --> 00:17:48,061
You're not gonna do much with that.

362
00:17:48,063 --> 00:17:50,640
I'm a bartender. Crowd
control's my thing.

363
00:17:51,038 --> 00:17:53,969
Hey, people? We got a little
situation on our hands here.

364
00:17:53,971 --> 00:17:55,211
Listen up.

365
00:17:55,670 --> 00:17:57,170
There's a woman trapped in the basement

366
00:17:57,172 --> 00:17:59,758
of that house over there.
Her husband's inside.

367
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:01,290
We could use some help.

368
00:18:03,210 --> 00:18:04,418
Yeah. All right.

369
00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:06,090
Yeah. I'll help.

370
00:18:06,092 --> 00:18:07,548
- I'm going.
- No, no, no. Just stay there.

371
00:18:07,550 --> 00:18:09,961
Hey, no. I need everyone
to stay by the bus.

372
00:18:09,963 --> 00:18:11,594
Well, there's a woman trapped in there.

373
00:18:11,596 --> 00:18:13,836
Then let emergency services handle it.

374
00:18:13,838 --> 00:18:15,649
Oh, you're a peach.

375
00:18:16,021 --> 00:18:18,149
Okay. Okay, look. You guys go.

376
00:18:18,151 --> 00:18:19,727
Listen. There are people on the way.

377
00:18:19,729 --> 00:18:21,102
They're gonna help everyone out, okay?

378
00:18:21,104 --> 00:18:22,961
They're gonna get everything
squared up. You're with...

379
00:18:22,963 --> 00:18:24,853
- Hey! Hey, no. Whoa.
- I'm going, too.

380
00:18:24,855 --> 00:18:28,242
They can't focus on your mom if
they're worried about you. Okay?

381
00:18:29,799 --> 00:18:32,499
Okay, come on. You're
needed here. Come with me.

382
00:18:35,090 --> 00:18:36,708
Remember, the most important thing is...

383
00:18:36,710 --> 00:18:38,719
Keep everybody calm. I know.

384
00:18:38,721 --> 00:18:41,171
Uh, you talk to the bus driver,
and I'll get everyone inside.

385
00:18:41,373 --> 00:18:43,422
- Let's go.
- Donna.

386
00:18:44,379 --> 00:18:46,129
We've got some problems.

387
00:18:46,131 --> 00:18:48,430
No shit. Where's the driver?

388
00:18:48,658 --> 00:18:51,883
Folks, sorry about
your inconvenience here.

389
00:18:51,885 --> 00:18:54,899
Let's get you all inside,
huh? Get some tea brewing.

390
00:18:54,901 --> 00:18:57,235
Get you all warmed up.

391
00:18:58,860 --> 00:19:00,094
Sounds like a good idea.

392
00:19:00,096 --> 00:19:02,516
- Right? Some tea sounds good.
- Uh-huh. Yeah.

393
00:19:02,518 --> 00:19:05,524
Come on in, guys. Please.

394
00:19:06,030 --> 00:19:07,750
Let's go, folks. Come on.

395
00:19:07,985 --> 00:19:09,320
Sorry again.

396
00:19:11,875 --> 00:19:13,625
Jim!

397
00:19:13,627 --> 00:19:15,067
Oh, thank God.

398
00:19:19,138 --> 00:19:20,578
Who are they?

399
00:19:21,059 --> 00:19:24,336
We, uh... our bus stopped here.

400
00:19:24,338 --> 00:19:26,360
- Your bus?
- Can you hear anything?

401
00:19:26,362 --> 00:19:28,320
- Is she talking?
- No.

402
00:19:29,308 --> 00:19:32,930
I, uh... no.

403
00:19:33,133 --> 00:19:36,310
What the fuck? What
was she doin' down here?

404
00:19:36,312 --> 00:19:38,735
JIM: Digging to see
where the wires went.

405
00:19:39,072 --> 00:19:40,502
It doesn't matter.

406
00:19:42,103 --> 00:19:43,468
If she was digging down here,

407
00:19:43,470 --> 00:19:45,440
what the hell caused that?

408
00:19:47,389 --> 00:19:49,016
Please just help me.

409
00:19:49,145 --> 00:19:52,255
Hey, bud, look at me. Look at me.

410
00:19:52,384 --> 00:19:55,063
We're gonna get your
lady out of there, okay?

411
00:19:56,345 --> 00:19:57,461
JIM: Wait, wait. Whoa, whoa, whoa.

412
00:19:57,463 --> 00:19:58,783
Before you lift anything out,

413
00:19:58,785 --> 00:20:01,765
just make sure that it's not
holding up somethin' else.

414
00:20:01,930 --> 00:20:04,524
Last thing we want is to
collapse things further.

415
00:20:04,662 --> 00:20:07,031
Okay. Yeah. We got this.

416
00:20:07,658 --> 00:20:09,711
Let's get this done quickly, alright?

417
00:20:11,817 --> 00:20:14,055
Yeah. Come here. Wait, wait, wait.

418
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:16,556
[VICTOR WHISPERING] Come.

419
00:20:19,706 --> 00:20:21,586
Come on.

420
00:20:21,701 --> 00:20:24,190
- Are you sure this is the right way?
- Shh.

421
00:20:30,916 --> 00:20:33,128
Oh, no, no, no. Victor.

422
00:20:33,130 --> 00:20:34,450
No, we have to keep going.

423
00:20:34,452 --> 00:20:35,971
No, no, no, Victor. We have to go back.

424
00:20:35,973 --> 00:20:38,713
No way. There's no going
back. We have to go through.

425
00:20:38,715 --> 00:20:41,605
That's what he said.
We go while they sleep.

426
00:20:41,925 --> 00:20:45,115
You have to be brave.
We both have to be brave.

427
00:20:53,608 --> 00:20:55,478
Sara?

428
00:20:59,365 --> 00:21:01,025
Sara, you up there?

429
00:21:03,035 --> 00:21:05,807
You said we'd be safe
inside this tree. [LAUGHING]

430
00:21:07,060 --> 00:21:11,525
Well, this does not feel
very safe to me, Sara.

431
00:21:14,930 --> 00:21:16,280
MAN: Hey.

432
00:21:21,683 --> 00:21:23,174
Hello?

433
00:21:27,540 --> 00:21:29,410
Hey, is anybody up there?

434
00:21:30,980 --> 00:21:32,730
[MAN IN THE DISTANCE] Are you real?

435
00:21:32,732 --> 00:21:33,782
What?

436
00:21:36,882 --> 00:21:39,205
MAN: Are you real?

437
00:21:40,217 --> 00:21:43,518
Yeah. Yeah, yeah, I'm real.

438
00:21:43,520 --> 00:21:46,060
Are you? Are you fuckin' real?

439
00:21:46,062 --> 00:21:49,088
MAN: I can help you if you help me.

440
00:21:49,090 --> 00:21:50,240
Okay.

441
00:21:50,578 --> 00:21:52,288
MAN: You promise?

442
00:21:52,290 --> 00:21:53,854
Yeah, man. Anything you want.

443
00:21:53,863 --> 00:21:57,103
Just please, just get
me outta here, man.

444
00:21:57,560 --> 00:21:59,580
MAN: You'll have to climb.

445
00:21:59,582 --> 00:22:00,822
What?

446
00:22:00,844 --> 00:22:02,514
No. I...

447
00:22:02,793 --> 00:22:05,089
[SHOUTS] I can't.

448
00:22:05,091 --> 00:22:07,011
I just... tried.

449
00:22:08,608 --> 00:22:10,471
MAN: Wait.

450
00:22:16,763 --> 00:22:18,666
BOYD: Hey. What... fuck!

451
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:21,180
What?

452
00:22:21,182 --> 00:22:24,549
MAN: You have to hurry.
They'll be back soon.

453
00:22:24,551 --> 00:22:28,205
Okay. All right. Uh, okay.

454
00:22:32,247 --> 00:22:33,647
CLARA: Hey.

455
00:22:36,732 --> 00:22:38,912
Do you think we made it angry?

456
00:22:39,127 --> 00:22:40,497
What are you talking about?

457
00:22:40,697 --> 00:22:42,717
That storm came out of nowhere,

458
00:22:42,719 --> 00:22:44,778
and the way the lights exploded,

459
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:46,920
it's almost like we
made something angry.

460
00:22:49,576 --> 00:22:50,706
What do we do now?

461
00:22:52,356 --> 00:22:54,361
Well...

462
00:22:55,053 --> 00:22:57,330
I got one rolling paper left...

463
00:22:58,150 --> 00:23:00,119
So I'm getting stoned.

464
00:23:02,500 --> 00:23:03,680
Okay.

465
00:23:11,111 --> 00:23:13,641
[OMINOUS SYNTHESIZER MUSIC PLAYS]

466
00:23:21,554 --> 00:23:23,408
[DUMMY SCREAMS]

467
00:23:25,238 --> 00:23:27,158
[SCREAMS]

468
00:23:35,876 --> 00:23:38,682
Okay. Okay.

469
00:23:48,462 --> 00:23:50,768
Here. I found this.

470
00:23:54,304 --> 00:23:56,198
There's a lot of broken glass.

471
00:23:56,301 --> 00:23:57,581
[SPEAKS CANTONESE]

472
00:23:57,601 --> 00:23:59,244
You careful.

473
00:24:01,917 --> 00:24:03,510
Why do you think they broke?

474
00:24:03,512 --> 00:24:05,622
That was scary.

475
00:24:05,915 --> 00:24:07,485
Very scary.

476
00:24:09,967 --> 00:24:12,447
Do you think the others
will be back soon?

477
00:24:14,770 --> 00:24:18,138
You don't be afraid. I protect you.

478
00:24:18,265 --> 00:24:19,615
I'm not afraid.

479
00:24:21,962 --> 00:24:25,385
Well, maybe a little afraid.

480
00:24:25,686 --> 00:24:28,006
Sometimes a quest can be scary.

481
00:24:28,245 --> 00:24:30,783
And when it gets close to the end,

482
00:24:31,409 --> 00:24:34,002
that's when it gets really scary.

483
00:24:35,012 --> 00:24:37,119
I guess we're sleeping here tonight?

484
00:24:38,950 --> 00:24:40,690
Whatever.

485
00:24:47,353 --> 00:24:48,843
What are you doing out here?

486
00:24:48,845 --> 00:24:50,375
Oh, for fuck's sake.

487
00:24:51,630 --> 00:24:53,346
Go back inside.

488
00:24:53,930 --> 00:24:55,460
Why?

489
00:24:55,597 --> 00:24:57,447
Because...

490
00:24:58,332 --> 00:25:00,315
You know, I don't know,
kid. Do whatever you want.

491
00:25:01,580 --> 00:25:04,020
You know cigarettes
are bad for you, right?

492
00:25:04,963 --> 00:25:06,703
It's not that kind of cigarette.

493
00:25:08,591 --> 00:25:10,510
What's wrong with you?

494
00:25:11,693 --> 00:25:12,893
Gee, I don't know.

495
00:25:12,895 --> 00:25:14,355
I mean... [CHUCKLES]

496
00:25:14,357 --> 00:25:15,729
maybe I just spent
the last week thinking

497
00:25:15,731 --> 00:25:18,231
we might actually get
out of this shit box,

498
00:25:18,233 --> 00:25:21,111
only to see our entire plan
come crashing down around us.

499
00:25:21,113 --> 00:25:22,458
Literally.

500
00:25:22,658 --> 00:25:24,858
So? We try again.

501
00:25:24,860 --> 00:25:26,205
Yeah.

502
00:25:26,207 --> 00:25:28,147
We'll get right on that, kid.

503
00:25:28,437 --> 00:25:30,486
Maybe we'll try something else.

504
00:25:30,488 --> 00:25:32,728
Whenever the Cromenockle
failed, he always found...

505
00:25:32,730 --> 00:25:34,791
What the fuck is a Cromenockle?

506
00:25:35,142 --> 00:25:37,672
- Oh. Um...
- No. I don't care.

507
00:25:39,400 --> 00:25:41,230
You're friends with Victor, right?

508
00:25:43,919 --> 00:25:45,471
Do you know which room is his?

509
00:25:46,410 --> 00:25:47,971
Why?

510
00:25:58,553 --> 00:26:01,773
[TABITHA WHISPERING] Okay. Shh.

511
00:26:08,088 --> 00:26:09,878
[VICTOR WHISPERING] Look. Right here.

512
00:26:21,879 --> 00:26:24,221
[GASPS] Let's go. Let's go. Let's go.

513
00:26:24,231 --> 00:26:26,893
Let's go. Let's go.
Please, please, let's go.

514
00:26:35,572 --> 00:26:37,205
TABITHA: Oh, my God.

515
00:26:41,330 --> 00:26:43,002
Oh, my God.

516
00:26:45,893 --> 00:26:48,104
- Victor?
- Shh.

517
00:27:03,252 --> 00:27:04,854
What?

518
00:27:05,512 --> 00:27:07,604
- No, Victor!
- Come on.

519
00:27:20,536 --> 00:27:24,229
Victor, Victor, Victor?

520
00:27:26,005 --> 00:27:28,775
Victor, Victor?

521
00:27:33,966 --> 00:27:35,796
Victor, which way?

522
00:27:38,979 --> 00:27:41,549
[PANTS] Victor?

523
00:27:42,518 --> 00:27:45,668
